The group of order 64 (a 2-group) acts on a set of size 21. By the orbit-stabilizer theorem, all orbits have sizes dividing 64 (i.e., powers of 2). If there were no fixed points, every orbit would have size at least 2, making the total number of elements even (sum of even numbers). However, 21 is odd, leading to a contradiction. Thus, there must be at least one fixed point.

**Final Answer**
\boxed{Yes}

